  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1107 PM MDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\nThe big upper low which helped bring some heavy rain to the area\nthe last couple days is going to lift out over the TX/OK\npanhandles Thursday morning. Light showers like what we saw today\nis expected for Thursday afternoon with showers moving north to\nsouth. Some light breezes will be seen Thursday afternoon out of\nthe northeast. A backdoor front will push in late Thursday and\nearly Friday morning shifting winds to the east and also bringing\nmuch breezier conditions. Wind speeds look to be anywhere from\n15-25 mph sustained that morning. Winds stay pretty breezy into\nthe afternoon hours Friday as well. Some drizzle possible in the \nSacramento Mtns, especially for east facing slopes. CAMs suggest \nmore widespread showery activity across the lowlands early that \nmorning. Saturday looks quiet with dry conditions and light winds.\nHeading into Sunday and early next weekend still looks uncertain.",
